target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestLoadsStructuralRulesThatNothingElseAsserts'
expect: a clean verdict forged by an unplaceable phase
why:    the sibling of the unknown-phase entry, for the WRONG-TYPED case. `phase` is decoded as json.RawMessage and then as a string precisely so a non-string phase reaches the switch; decoding it as a string in the envelope makes the whole envelope fail, and the row then vanishes down the torn-line path with no error — forging the same clean verdict. The two halves need separate entries because they fail in different places: this one before the switch, the other in its default arm.
--- old
		var phase string
		if err := json.Unmarshal(env.Phase, &phase); err != nil {
			r.setErr(lineNo, "unreadable-phase", fmt.Errorf(
				"phase is absent or not a string, so the row's fields cannot be placed: %w", err))
			continue
		}
--- new
		var phase string
		if json.Unmarshal(env.Phase, &phase) != nil {
			continue
		}
